Z||000000||engine18||08-30-2000||06:49 AM||||I'm attempting to upgrade my wheels and a great deal cross my path... Will these wheels fit my 84 2m4?  <BR>15 X 6  5 lug with a 30mm offset<BR>with 5 by 100mm bolt pattern.....<BR>Thanks for any help....<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000001||mrfixit58||08-30-2000||10:57 AM||||Sounds right to me.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||the need for speed||08-30-2000||12:06 PM||||what does the off set mean, and does any offset fit a fiero how, do you tell what off set you need???||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||08-30-2000||04:26 PM||||Offset is the distance off center the wheel is relative the face of the hub.<P>Yes it matters what the offset is.<P>The offset you need depends on the wheels. wheels wider than OE will need diferant offsets to clear things in the wheel well.<P><A HREF="http://www.americanracing.com/" TARGET=_blank>American Racing</A> has a nice FAQ that explains most terms in plain english.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-30-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierocrazy||08-30-2000||05:03 PM||||i am sure 30mm is right, have to be careful of the toe in/toe out knuckle if you try to got in more... ( i try to run my car with no rear discs on it and they rims rubber )  ooppss||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierosound||09-08-2000||12:27 AM||||To see the many styles of aftermarket wheels are now available, check out the website below.  I LOVE the wire wheels, but I'm not sure how they'd look on a Fiero... any comments?<BR> <A HREF="http://www.salesco.com/wheels/advantage/74_advantage__custom_wheel.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.salesco.com/wheels/advantage/74_advantage__custom_wheel.htm</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000006||BroCar 87||09-08-2000||12:43 AM||||Sorry guys, I don't think they will fit. The 84 2m4 came with AT LEAST a 35mm offset. If the stock rims are the 14", the offset is 35mm. If the stock rims were 13", the offset was 42mm.<BR>ANY 15" or 16" rim with a 35mm offset AND a bolt pattern of 5 x 100mm will fit the 84-87 Fiero.<BR>Are the rims aftermarket or stock from a different car? <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NorthFLFieroSIG.jpg">      <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>84 SE (project)<P>[This message has been edited by BroCar 87 (edited 09-08-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by BroCar 87 (edited 09-08-2000).]||||reg||11
